    "body": "## AI-Generated Details\n\nPrepared with Codex from the author's capacity-factor requirement.\n\nTwo eager chunks must not each allocate a full-call HybridEP output budget.\nDerive one absolute row bound:\n\n```text\nB = max_input_tokens * ep_size * min(local_experts, top_k) * capacity_factor\nchunk0 = floor(B / 2)\nchunk1 = B - floor(B / 2)\n```\n\nApply native alignment to each half, then bind that integer while tracing the\nchunk. The public dispatcher factor is unchanged and replay does not consult\nthe Python context. Factor4 therefore becomes effective factor2 per chunk on\nthe same full-call basis; do not halve both the token bound and the factor.\nTransport buffers are a separate shared allocation, not this output capacity.\n\n## Test Plan\n\nThe real native contract family covers allocated bytes, alignment, retained\nrouting state and deliberate capacity drops. Final-stack traced dispatches\nuse the expected static row bounds, and deterministic same-chunk training\nmatched exact loss/norm and full checkpoint state. No host token-size read is\nintroduced. Those tests ran through the production backend, not a patched\nallocation or a synthetic FX graph.\n\nThis capacity policy applies to SPMD token chunks. The separate PP feature\ndoes not chunk tokens and preserves each microbatch's full capacity factor.\n",
